  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/chaetobranchopsis-australis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Chaetobranchopsis australis is a cichlid from Paraguay specialised in feeding on small planktonic organisms. It grows up to 12–14 cm long.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/chaetobranchopsis-australis-2/",
      "html": "<p>The fish swallows water like a vacuum cleaner and sieves the plankton out of it with long gill rakers. At the time of importation (last September) plankton in Paraguay was rather rare, so the fish were skinnier than desired.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/chaetobranchopsis-australis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Chaetobranchopsis is one of the very few cichlid genera whose breeding behaviour is completely unknown. Aquarium fish have been observed cleaning stones, so they might be open brooders, but this is not known.</p>"
    }
  ],
